  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The `habeas:coverage` citation on `format_node_content` in the `GraphWithChangingEdges` test fixture is justified.\n\n- **It is on an explicit function with a body, in fenced commentary.** The built-in allows a coverage exception for such a function.\n- **The reason is substantive and matches the test.** In `agent_edge_tools_record_selections_without_validating_targets`, the scripted agent calls only `outgoing_edges` and then `submit_result`. The test asserts that the recorded dependency is `Dependency::OutgoingEdges` and nothing else, so this fixture's `format_node_content` is never meant to run. The panic in its body is a guard. A real rendering would introduce a content input that the test forbids.\n- **The commentary agrees with the library code.** In `crates/habeas-sdk/src/agent/tools.rs`, `dispatch` calls `format_node_content` only when the agent uses the node-reading tool. In `crates/habeas-sdk/src/procedure.rs`, `Ask::execute` calls it only to prepare explicit inputs. Neither happens in this edge-only test.\n- **The claim about other tests holds.** Other tests in `crates/habeas-sdk/tests/agent.rs` use `Memory`'s `Domain::format_node_content` with custom formatters: `concurrent_tool_agents_isolate_histories_pages_and_submissions_and_share_reads`, `validator_agent_executions_isolate_conversations_and_dependency_traces` and `node_rendering_tool_errors_allow_recovery_without_recording_undelivered_contents`. They exercise rendering with explicitly requested contents.\n- **No other citation rule is violated.** The citation is a `{cite}` of a built-in, so there is no redundant `{impl}` or `{test}` reference to check.",
